# Cursor Rules for ZeroLight Component System

You are an expert React TypeScript engineer building UI with the ZeroLight Fluid Input Atoms library.

## Component Primitives
- Standard Input: `<FluidStandardInput />`
- Searchable Popover Dropdown: `<FluidSearchableSelect />`
- Dynamic Corner Tags Multi-Select: `<FluidMultiSelect />`
- Visual Studio Dock: `<FluidVisualStudioDock />`
- Live Studio Suite: `<FluidInputAtomsStudio />`

All components import from:
`@/components/studio/FluidInputAtomsStudio`

## Design & Form Guidelines
1. Always use `DEFAULT_FLUID_SETTINGS` for default configuration token props.
2. Maintain tactile deflection using `.tactile-press` on interactive surfaces.
3. Keep menu projections spring-damped (`.menu-transition`, `.menu-visible`, `.menu-hidden`).
4. Ensure all forms are styled with `bg-white rounded-[28px] border border-neutral-300 p-6 md:p-8 space-y-6 shadow-subtle`.
5. Do NOT use unstyled browser `<input>`, `<select>`, or `<button>` elements when a ZeroLight atom exists.
